# Build-context excludes for `docker build` from the repository root.
#
# The Docker log-driver plugin's rootfs image (crates/imbh-server/docker-plugin/Dockerfile) builds
# from the repo root, because compiling `imbhd` needs the whole Cargo workspace -- every member
# manifest, not just crates/imbh-server. That makes `COPY . .` read the entire tree.
#
# Without this file the context includes `target/` and `.agents-workspace/`, which in a working
# checkout are *hundreds of gigabytes* of build artifacts and scratch data. Docker hashes and
# transfers the context before running the first instruction, so the build appears to hang
# indefinitely with no output rather than failing. The sources themselves are a few megabytes.

# Cargo build artifacts. Gitignored (ARCHITECTURE.md section 12); routinely 100 GB+.
target/
**/target/

# Agent scratch space (AGENTS.md): probe crates, temporary target dirs, fixtures.
.agents-workspace/

# Version-control metadata and CI definitions -- not needed to compile.
.git/
.github/

# rustfmt backups.
**/*.rs.bk
